# Anatomy kit — attribution and provenance

The isometric SVG toolkit in this directory (`iso-kit.ts`, `draw.tsx`,
`live.tsx`) is **adapted** from the `anatomy` project by Ryan
(https://github.com/wheresryan22/anatomy), which is published under the MIT
License. The MIT License permits reuse and modification provided the copyright
and permission notice are preserved.

## What was imported

| File here | Upstream origin | Change |
|---|---|---|
| `iso-kit.ts` | `kit/iso-kit.ts` | verbatim (blob-verified — see provenance) |
| `draw.tsx` | `kit/react/draw.tsx` | import path `../iso-kit` → `./iso-kit` (only change) |
| `live.tsx` | `kit/react/live.tsx` | verbatim (blob-verified) |
| `iso-kit.mjs` | `kit/iso-kit.mjs` | verbatim (runtime dep of lathe/tube) |
| `lathe.mjs` | `kit/lathe.mjs` | verbatim — turned solids (`lathe`/`solidOf`/`sphereOf`/`disc`/`ringBand`) |
| `tube.mjs` | `kit/tube.mjs` | verbatim (pipes/cables; vendored for future use) |

The bespoke reference figure that upstream ships alongside the kit
(`model.mjs`, `build.mjs`, `kit/lathe.mjs`, `kit/tube.mjs`, `kit/gl.mjs`,
`kit/turn*.mjs`, `kit/audit.mjs`, `kit/canvas-painter.mjs`, `iso.css`, and the
generated `eclipse-refinery.html`) is NOT imported into the app runtime. It
remains under `docs/figures/eclipse-refinery/` as a reference/quality benchmark
only.

## Update procedure

1. Diff the upstream `kit/iso-kit.ts`, `kit/react/draw.tsx` and
   `kit/react/live.tsx` against these files.
2. Re-apply the import-path edit in `draw.tsx`.
3. Re-run `npm run test` and `npx tsc --noEmit` from `Black-Eclipse-site/`.
4. Record the upstream commit hash below when bumping.

